    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 23rd with a lineup heavily leveraged toward high-leverage spots against right-handed pitching. Our strongest play of the day is **Yordan Alvarez** (76.31), whose elite xwOBA of 0.419 and a favorable matchup against Rea (R) make him the anchor of our offense. Right behind him, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.19) provide exceptional value; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically gains significant ground due to his dynamic platoon advantage and leadoff spot, while **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive 19% boost derived from the favorable SP_xERA of Roki Sasaki. Despite a \"wind in\" warning affecting the sluggers, the stolen base upside inherent in **Trea Turner** (68.35) remains essential to our 5x5 strategy, as his leadoff status and the slow delivery of Cecconi (R) provide the highest efficiency path for a multi-category boost today.\n\nManaging the bench remains a high-stakes balancing act, especially with the weather-induced exclusions of **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith** due to rainouts. Among those available, **Carson Benge** (48.91) barely held his spot in the lineup over our reserve depth, largely due to the optimization of his leadoff position despite a challenging matchup against Meyer. While **Hyeseong Kim** and **Casey Schmitt** sit at the bottom of our active rotation, they remain in the lineup over reserves like **Caleb Durbin** or **Kazuma Okamoto** because their confirmed role\u2014even at the bottom of the order\u2014provides more projected efficiency than the uncertainty of bench options. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez** closely; his 55.52 score relies heavily on the poor xERA of his opponent, and we must confirm the lineup to ensure he isn't rested, which would trigger a pivot to the versatility provided by **Josh Smith** or **Dillon Dingler**. With **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** waiting in the wings, the Zebras are well-positioned to shift if late-breaking lineup changes emerge.",
